0..34 Comment "/// A transport along a held call."
35..38 Comment "///"
39..115 Comment "/// A composite whose second path is a stuck call is one composite. The call"
116..181 Comment "/// may stand alone or behind an identity, and the kernel agrees."
182..185 Comment "///"
186..255 Comment "/// The append runs a held operand and writes a bind over its call. A"
256..330 Comment "/// transport along the held path is a bind over the same call. So the two"
331..398 Comment "/// compare by the call, then by the transports under one variable."
399..402 Comment "///"
403..501 Comment "/// - see: #3800 — the checker declined two composites that differ only by a call of an identity"
503..545 Comment "/// The identity on paths from `x` to `y`."
